{
  "id": "find-the-duplicate-number",
  "questionId": "find-the-duplicate-number",
  "slug": "find-the-duplicate-number",
  "title": "Find the Duplicate Number",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Fast slow pointers",
  "patterns": [
    "fast & slow pointers",
    "cycle detection",
    "array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "sorting or a hash set would work but both cost you either the no-modification rule or the O(1) space rule - think about what property forces a 'collision' here: values are in [1,n] but there are n+1 of them",
    "imagine building a sequence by starting at index 0 and repeatedly jumping to index nums[current] - since a value repeats, two different indices point into the same place, which means this sequence must eventually revisit a node. what does that remind you of?",
    "this is exactly a linked list with a cycle, where the duplicate value is the entry point of the cycle - use fast/slow pointers to find where fast and slow first meet",
    "once fast and slow meet, reset one pointer to index 0 (the start) and advance both one step at a time as index-jumps - where they meet again is the duplicate value, following the same logic as finding a cycle's start"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using a hash set or sorting, which breaks the O(1) space or no-modification constraint",
    "confusing values and indices when doing the jump nums[current], since values are 1-indexed but array indices are 0-indexed",
    "returning the fast/slow meeting point value directly instead of doing the second phase to find the actual cycle entrance"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array `nums` of n + 1 integers where every value is\nbetween 1 and n inclusive. There is exactly one value that is repeated;\nit may appear more than twice, and other values may or may not all be\npresent.\n\n**Find the repeated value, without modifying the array and using only O(1) extra space.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= n <= 10^5, nums.length == n + 1",
      "1 <= nums[i] <= n",
      "exactly one value is duplicated, but it may appear more than twice, and not every value in [1,n] needs to appear",
      "the array must not be modified, and only O(1) extra space is allowed"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the duplicate value appears more than twice",
      "the duplicate is the smallest possible value (1) or the largest (n)",
      "the minimal case n = 1 with nums = [1, 1]"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
